# Strategy Validation Gates

- This repository uses validation gates as evidence requirements inside the existing status machine, not as a parallel state system. Status labels remain defined only in `docs/research-governance/strategy-status-glossary.md`.
- Gate details, default thresholds, report expectations, and allowed deviations live in `docs/research-governance/strategy-validation-gates.md`. Do not copy the full checklist into core ledgers, README routing tables, or AGENTS.md.
- Registration/freeze and promotion are distinct operations: `explore -> registered` fixes version identity and evidence links only. “登记/冻结 Vx” never means “promote Vx”.
- At registration, record known gate gaps without automatically running the full review.
- Before `registered -> live spec`, complete one promotion review covering all research-side gates (excess-return baseline, ablation, OOS/CPCV), live-readiness gates (Monte Carlo robustness, stress tests, phase/bar-alignment sensitivity), and the existing live-executable audit. Missing or failed evidence keeps the version at `registered / not promoted / not live-ready`.
- Statistical significance (PSR/DSR/MinTRL) and start-time sensitivity are optional diagnostics, not hard blockers. Historical reports that scored old gates 5/6/7 keep their contemporaneous numbering.
- `live spec -> dry-run -> live` remains governed by the runner handoff, runner-tracking, and operations rules in `lab-runner-handoff.mdc` and `live-executable-strategy-research.mdc`. `dry-run -> live` additionally requires a completed online open/close reconciliation report comparing runtime fills against backtest expectations (see `lab-runner-handoff.mdc`); offline parity alone is insufficient.
- Gate thresholds are default repository standards, not immutable constants. A report may use a stricter or different threshold only when it states why the default is unsuitable, what replacement was used, and records the deviation in the family `decision-log.md`.
- Do not treat unavailable data as a pass. For example, if phase testing needs `1m` candles and they are missing, record the gate as incomplete and keep the version `not promoted / not live-ready`.
- Gate evidence belongs under the relevant family directory: durable Markdown in `diagnostics/`, `ablations/`, or `notes/` by nature; scripts in `scripts/`; retained JSON/CSV/plots in `artifacts/`; state changes in `decision-log.md`; compact links and status in the core ledger.
- Existing dry-run or historical versions are not automatically downgraded by this rule. Apply these gates to new promotion attempts and to any later attempt to move an existing version toward `live`.
